  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is clearly the dominant modality (config_001: 0.485 vs config_010 image-only: 0.208), and multiprofile + avgpool with PCA gave a strong boost (config_002: 0.591 vs config_001: 0.485). However, all three completed experiments used PCA_n2000 as the RNA encoder, leaving the most fundamental design axis—RNA representation quality—completely untested. Uncertainty: We do not know whether a learned encoder (scvi_n200) captures more discriminative biological signal than a linear PCA projection, and this choice will govern all downstream multimodal experiments. What this tests: config_005 changes exactly one variable from config_002 (PCA → scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile + avgpool), giving a clean A/B comparison of encoder quality. Why this is the best use of budget: The RNA encoder is the highest-leverage design decision because RNA is the dominant signal source; resolving whether a learned representation meaningfully outperforms PCA will determine whether subsequent multimodal experiments should invest in scvi/scgpt or stick with PCA, and it reduces the effective search space more than testing aggregation (transformer vs avgpool) would, since avgpool already performs well."
